          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Have a flush consisting of more cards than the dealer's flush. If the card counts are equal, the higher-ranking cards within the flush win.",
          gameplay: '1. Players place an **Ante** bet.\n2. Both player and dealer are dealt 7 cards.\n3. Players either **Fold** (lose Ante) or **Raise** based on their hand.\n4. **Raise Amounts**:\n   - 4-card flush or lower: Raise = 1x Ante.\n   - 5-card flush: Raise = Up to 2x Ante.\n   - 6 or 7-card flush: Raise = Up to 3x Ante.\n5. Dealer reveals their hand. The dealer must **Qualify** with at least a 3-card 9-high flush.',
          keyRules: [
            'Dealer qualifies with at least 3-card flush 9-high.',
            'Raise cap: 1x ante (two- to four-card max flush), 2x (five-card), 3x (six- or seven-card).',
            'Win by having more cards in your longest flush than dealer, or higher rank within same length.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Always raise if you have a 3-card J-10-2 flush or better. The house edge is optimized by folding Very weak hands.',
          intermediate: "Follow the 'Wizard of Odds' strategy: Fold any 3-card flush lower than 9-8-2. Play all 3-card flushes 9-high or higher.",
          advanced: "Always make the maximum allowed Raise for 5, 6, or 7-card flushes, as they are strong favorites against the dealer's qualifying hand.",
          tips: [
            'The side bets have a significantly higher house edge than the main game. Use them sparingly.',
            'The dealer only qualifies about 75% of the time, so even a mediocre 3-card flush can win when the dealer fails to qualify.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
